  "body": "**Description:** \r\n\r\nWhen using SSO as only sign-in method, having the local login confuses users. E.g. on mobile, they need to scroll down and see the \"log in with ... \" SSO buttons and use those. Overriding templates only for this is inconvenient, especially when using a Docker deployment which relies on mounting in additional files. \r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1991377/158067718-7522bdf2-e4c6-4c66-be7c-24e77ebdec5e.png)\r\n\r\nIn this image the SSO buttons are missing images for unknown reasons... but you get the idea :)) It would be ideal if clients could respond to a \"hide local login\" config knob and then make that happen on the client side of things. I'm using Element myself.\r\n\r\nFollowing the config in https://matrix-org.github.io/synapse/latest/sample_config.yaml, I think a `hide_local: true/false` might fit under the `sso: ...` stanza as it matches the description of \"Additional settings to use with single-sign on systems such as OpenID Connect ...\".",
